aching the window he  closed it he knew my previous strategy  and forced me to adapt every other  leader once i got into a groove i could  kill them the same way every time  sneaking in through the ducks climb the  stairs link everyone in the room and  sneak out without anyone knowing it's  actually recommended that to outsmart  him you change your gear constantly like  using different guns or abilities  because of this though i had to find a  new way inside this is when i discovered  a small window which is connected to the  room charlie is located in i thought  this was a perfect time for a grenade  and while it didn't kill him it opened  me up to another idea down the path to  charlie's playroom is an elevated  walkway as i walked over i noticed that  charlie's room could be seen from here  so i immediately rushed back to the  bunker skipped time to the middle of the  night so i could grab igor's sniper  after retrieving the sniper i returned  back at noon and attempted to put my  idea to the test after looking around it  didn't seem like i was in a position to  even shoot him and i figured that he  probably wouldn't die either since he  has way more health than many of the  other npcs in the game i'll admit i felt  a little defeated as he was the one  leader i couldn't kill creatively or  quickly at all so i was determined to  figure something out i thought maybe a  change of abilities could help this  charlie when killed drops the shift slab  which is essentially blink from  dishonored every time a leader is killed  they will drop their respective slabs  and even upgrades to the same slab so i  ran through a couple times killing him  and making sure i got the shift slab and  anything i needed to start devising more  plans whenever charlie is alerted he'll  scream and run into his room and when  you confront him in the room he runs  back into the main building i actually  had him tricked at one point in an  earlier loop by hacking the turrets in  his room to kill him which is what  sparked this idea the problem is that i  hacked him when he was already inside i  wanted him to walk into his room and be  blasted right away he is a lot smarter  than i thought and is incredibly  paranoid and protective of his things he  seems to be the type of person that  notices when something of his was moved  because every time whether it was the  turrets or trip mines the moment he  notices something's wrong he bolts so  this plane was an entire bust i decided  to revisit the window again but now with  blink i might be able to do it but the  problem is that there was only one spot  nearby that i could even reach with  blink and even with the upgraded ability  to hover shortly i still could line this  up i had one idea left and if this  didn't work then i was out of options  the windows on the top floor maybe i  could jump off the roof and hover so  that i could be right in line with the  window so that it'd be easier to land on  this would allow me to sneak through the  window and kill him without being  spotted  [Music]  after 45 minutes of trying and failing i  prevailed i was finally able to defeat  charlie without getting caught or  needing to start a firefight to kill him  and it felt great and the fact that i  tried this much as a compliment to the  game's design this is what i've always  appreciated about dishonored because of  how intricate these levels are 9 times  out of 10 if you have an idea or a  different route you could more than  likely do it death loop is the same way  and honestly for a good while it felt  like i was playing dishonored again and  that was a genuinely wonderful feeling  it took all the wonderful elements that  i loved about dishonored and evolved  them in such a way that it was a blast  to play i want to reiterate charlie is  not the only one that is this expansive  just about every leader is engaging to  fight and allows you to come up with  numerous routes and plans to increase  your enjoyment as you go from one  strategy to another for example alexis  is hosting a party with dozens of  eternalists except all of them are  wearing the same wolf mask so you can't  tell where he is just like we have to  come up with new routes and ideas thanks  to 2-bit with alexis we don't have to  worry about that problem but we have  other issues at hand we don't know where  he is as he looks the same as everyone  another example is the leader frank his  area is actually quite easy to navigate  honestly but the biggest caveat is that  his area is only accessible via a class  pass and when you equip the class pass  you lose all of your slabs meaning  repraise is no longer going to revive  you after death so by one mistake you'll  be back at the beach in the morning  because every leader is so unique to  each other and given a location that is  just as unique as themselves with each  of them having different problems for  the player to overcome it makes these  areas so much fun to play every single  time whether it's the first loop or the  tenth and by switching out your normal  equipment with guns and abilities that  are out of your comfort zone it makes  the encounter seem new again like in the  charlie example because my abilities  were changed my way of thinking changed  because now i had different limits than  before i couldn't reach this gap or this  jump without blink so instead of walking  through the front door and scaling the  stairs like normal i was able to take a  different route and while i know the  layout of the map and remember the enemy  placement it still felt different as i  was approaching it from a different  angle it's such wonderful game design  and truly the best part of the game  eventually though you may find yourself  a bit bored maybe you really don't want  to change your play style or you've done  everything that you can think of and it  becomes too easy arcane solves this  problem with juliana while the seven  leaders are the antagonists of the story  